{
  "name": "Counterparty MTM valuations for auditors",
  "today": "Counterparties that trade derivatives with Enron must show their auditors third-party valuations of those positions. Confirmations (Larry Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) answers these requests but has no system that values the deals. So each request is emailed to the five gas desk heads. Each desk head forwards it to an analyst on the desk, who runs a mini-book for that counterparty as of the year-end date, exports it to Excel, blacks out Delta/Vol and sends it back. The desk head then passes the answer on, and the regional answers are put together. In one example (Tudor BVI and Osprey) the West desk alone took four hand-offs and over an hour: Gossett sent the request at 9:54, Giron forwarded it to Carole Frank at 9:57, she replied at 11:05, and Giron forwarded her reply to Gossett at 11:13. The same thing happens in every region.",
  "change": "Give Confirmations a counterparty valuation report with stored year-end and month-end curves, so they can answer audit requests without going to the desks.",
  "explanation": "Build the tool Confirmations already asked for: EnTelligence, or a standard report on the official books, that keeps back-dated curves. It would show MTM and notional by counterparty short name across all regions, and would leave out Delta/Vol so nothing has to be blacked out. Confirmations would run it themselves for the counterparty and date, then send the result to the counterparty's auditor. Desk heads and Risk analysts would drop out of the loop: no forwarding, no mini-books, no blacking out, no putting regional answers together.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000.  If you can export into \nexcel and forward by e-mail, that would be appreciated."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "Confirmations has no valuation system, so each request uses up a Risk analyst's time and involves blacking out Delta/Vol. The tool they want would remove both steps."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Until we can get EnTelligence built to our specifications, \nwe'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Every request goes out to all the desks."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "Each region answers separately, and the answers then have to be put together."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "The total MTM value \nfor the West Desk are as follows.  Detail can be found in the attachment.",
      "note": "The analyst's reply came at 11:05 to a request forwarded at 9:57, and the desk head then relayed it at 11:13. That is four hand-offs for one region."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 3,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 75
}

