{
  "name": "Monthly sweep to flip ECC master-swap deals into FT-US/CAND-ERMS",
  "today": "When Enron Canada (ECC) has a master swap agreement with a counterparty, that counterparty's deals must settle between ECC and the counterparty in the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book. EOL and TAGG still book many of them into Houston books as ENA deals. Stacey Vallejo in Calgary finds some by hand and emails deal lists to the Houston desk heads. Before each monthly Nymex close she also asks 7 to 8 desk heads to search all their books. Each desk head forwards the request to their book administrators (Darron Giron forwards it to 2 to 7 analysts), who search and flip the deals. Each desk builds its own search. Between sweeps she sends one-off flip requests, about 20 to one desk head in 7 months. Deals that are missed break invoicing and liquidations, which then have to be re-run.",
  "change": "Book deals with ECC master-swap counterparties to FT-US/CAND-ERMS automatically, and replace the all-desk monthly sweep with one exception query.",
  "explanation": "Extend the EOL auto-booking rule that already exists for TransCanada Energy and Dynegy Canada to every counterparty with an ECC master swap (for example Duke Energy Marketing LP and Aquila Canada Corp.). In TAGG, add a check that flags any deal with a counterparty on the ECC master-swap list that is booked outside FT-US/CAND-ERMS, either blocking the save or listing it on a daily exception query. Before each Nymex close Stacey Vallejo runs that query and fixes or requests only the deals it lists. Desk heads and book administrators no longer search every book each month, and missed deals are caught before invoicing rather than after liquidations.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/360.eml",
      "quote": "Just a friendly reminder for you to please go through all your books to make"
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/292.eml",
      "quote": "Please go through your books to see if \nthere are any deals that I might have missed."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/195.eml",
      "quote": "This is just a quick reminder for all of you to please go into all of your \nbooks and flip out all the deals that are supposed to settle with ECC and a \nthird counterparty  to the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book by the end of the day today."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/108.eml",
      "quote": "What I'm \nrequesting is that you go through all your books and look for all deals with \nAquila\nCanada Corp."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/195.eml",
      "quote": "Nymex closes today, and we need to make sure that all the deals are booked \ncorrectly for both the Calgary and Houston offices.",
      "note": "The sweep is tied to the monthly Nymex close. Stacey sent it to 8 desk heads, and Giron forwarded it to 7 analysts, each of whom searches their books."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/360.eml",
      "quote": "Goss said you may have a calc set up to identify these deals.  Any chance I \ncould copy it?",
      "note": "There is no shared tool. Each desk finds these deals its own way."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/292.eml",
      "quote": "I've spoken to Jennifer Denny with EOL about getting a \nprogram set up for Duke deals similar to ones we have with TransCanada Energy \nand Dynegy Canada so they automatically get booked to settle with ECC, but I \ndon't think this has happened yet.",
      "note": "Automatic booking already exists for two counterparties. The change extends it to the rest."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/108.eml",
      "quote": "These deals would not have shown up when\nyou looked for deals to flip to the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book as they aren't in\nTAGG as ECC deals.",
      "note": "Searching by hand misses deals booked as ENA. A check keyed on the counterparty list would catch them."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/168.eml",
      "quote": "This is causing problems with the \nFebruary Liquidations as I settled this deal with Aquila, but it isn't coming\nthrough the liquidations correctly.",
      "note": "Rework when a deal is missed: the liquidations have to be re-run. This is not counted in the minutes."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/407.eml",
      "quote": "Could you please \nmake sure that there aren't any more deals with ECC and a third counterparty \nin this book as it messes up invoicing and settlement.",
      "note": "A one-off request between sweeps, here for 12 deals in MGMT-WEST."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 250
}

